    "q-140124": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140124",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ k \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -k-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that  $u⊥v.$ Find the value of $k.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 3+k\\cdot (-k-1)+k\\cdot (-7)+3\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =21-{k}^{2}-k-7k-36 \\\\  & =-{k}^{2}-8k-15 \\\\  & =-({k}^{2}+8k+15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({k}^{2}+8k+15) & =0 \\\\ -(k+5)(k+3) & =0 \\\\ k & =-5,-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
